body:
Hey there, thanks for opening this issue. There is a much simpler solution to that :) I'm not quite sure to understand what you're trying to achieve with the jQuery code, but I can help with how to programmatically update the index:

The search parameters are handled by a specific library called the Helper. One of this parameter is the index. In order to change the index, you just need to access the instance of the helper, modify the current index and trigger a new search. The best way to access the Helper is to create a new [custom widget](https://community.algolia.com/instantsearch.js/v2/guides/custom-widget.html). In the widget you can do the rendering and DOM manipulation operations you need (like adding a new onClick handler to a specific element).

```js
search.addWidget({
  init: function({helper}) {
    $('#someElement').click(function() {
      helper.setIndex('someIndex').search();
    });
  }
});
```
